 "card_notes": [
  {
   "text": "- **Context length**: 32,768 tokens",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct README.md:L64"
  },
  {
   "text": "### Chat Template",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct README.md:L83"
  },
  {
   "text": "LFM2.5 uses a ChatML-like format. See the [Chat Template documentation](https://docs.liquid.ai/lfm/key-concepts/chat-template) for details. Example:",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct README.md:L85"
  },
  {
   "text": "You can use [`tokenizer.apply_chat_template()`](https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/en/chat_templating#using-applychattemplate) to format your messages automatically.",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct README.md:L95"
  },
  {
   "text": "1. **Function definition**: We recommend providing the list of tools as a JSON object in the system prompt. You can also use the [`tokenizer.apply_chat_template()`](https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/en/chat_extras#passing-tools) function with tools.",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct README.md:L101"
  },
  {
   "text": "2. **Function call**: By default, LFM2.5 writes Pythonic function calls (a Python list between `<|tool_call_start|>` and `<|tool_call_end|>` special tokens), as the assistant answer. You can override this behavior by asking the model to output JSON function calls in the system prompt.",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct README.md:L102"
  },
  {
   "text": "tokenizer, generation defaults, and the same chat template as the released QAD GGUF.",
   "source": "LiquidAI/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct-GGUF README.md:L74"
  }
